  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 78647,
  "published": "2026-08-25T23:16:13.55Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 12.1.3 - Fixed blob URL parsing (ParseBlobUrl) that could produce an empty blob name and throw\n\t\tArgumentException(\"Value cannot be an empty string. (Parameter 'blobName')\") on Delete/Download/SAS\n\t\toperations. The parser now resolves the container and blob relative to the configured Account.Uri\n\t\tinstead of guessing the layout from the host, which handles Azurite endpoints with or without an\n\t\taccount path segment as well as cloud endpoints uniformly.\n\n\t\tPrevious Release (12.1.2):\n\t\t- updated nuget package dependencies to latest versions (Azure.Storage.Blobs, Azure.Storage.Files.Shares, Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions, Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection, Microsoft.Extensions.Logging, Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ConfigurationExtensions)\n\n\n\t\tPrevious Release (12.1.1):\n\t\t- Added SAS (Shared Access Signature) generation for blobs and containers.\n\t\t- GetBlobSasUriAsync(container, blobName, ...) and GetBlobSasUriAsync(url, ...) return a full, time-limited download URL for a blob.\n\t\t- GetContainerSasUriAsync(container, ...) returns a full, time-limited container URL.\n\t\t- GetBlobSasTokenAsync(...) and GetContainerSasTokenAsync(...) return only the SAS token query string that can be appended to any blob URL.\n\t\t- SAS generation is auth-aware: account-key signing for ConnectionString/DevelopmentStorage and User Delegation SAS for ManagedIdentity/UserToken.",
